# V5 historical admission

This component replays the unchanged twelve v2/v3 cases and selects the one
completed v4 C2 cost rejection. The v4 coordinator remains `failed`; both v4
suite receipts remain `input-changed`. Their interrupted final inventory scans
are retained as errors. A new read-only inventory comparison supplies a current
observation, never an invented historical `immutable_inputs_after`.

`review(base, generation, proof, original_verifier, expected)` returns the exact
previous twelve-case result after invoking its pinned independent checker.
`admit_v4_c2_cost(base, proof, original_verifier, expected)` authenticates the
original construction, complete new verifier, protected output, recorded resource
bounds, process retirement, restricted prelude and later diagnostic retirement.
Its result is `trident/selected-v4-cost-rejection/v1`,
`passed-selected-v4-cost`, generation2. It includes the exact rejection, original
proof/profile, literal failed suite/controller statuses, verification,
construction admission, retirement and prelude references, the reconstructed
prelude identity, source manifest, current immutable inputs and quiescence.

The selected case requires no deleted diagnostic body and grants no deletion.
No process, proof workload, network request or cleanup is launched. Original
positive proof identity and caller verification are freshly authenticated by the
pinned prior checker. Numerical limits and twenty-three-case contract stay fixed.
